    "snippet": "* Rain and storm chances return Saturday afternoon and Sunday as moisture surges northward * Drier conditions for Labor Day, monsoonal moisture and warmer temperatures may return mid next week. This combined with a mid-upper shortwave moving north from the Pacific into the CRV will provide enough lift to spark off an area of showers and isolated convection beginning Saturday in the CRV and Mohave County, then expanding in coverage and spreading northward Sunday over much San Bernardino and Clark",
    "source": "NWS Las Vegas Area Forecast Discussion"
